			<td class="log_table_head">■ <strong>ついにPALにもDEF？</strong> </td>
			<td align="right" class="log_table_head">2004年04月06日（火）</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td class="log_table_data" colspan="2">
				<br>
				<table width="100%">
					<tr>
						<td class="log_table_indent">&nbsp;</td>
						<td><a href="javascript:void(0)" onClick="window.open('./diary.cgi?mode=img&file=66.jpeg&width=640&height=516&byte=68,612', 'Img', 'width=640,height=516')"><img src="./upfile/66.jpeg" alt="68,612 byte" border="0" width="200" height="161"></a><br><br>おぉ！！　ついにPAL/SK最強（いまもテクニカル<br>クラスとして最強だと思います）<br><br>大胆なアップグレードだぁ、と思いながら<br>日付が４月１日だったりするけど、コレ本当？<br><br>Over the last several months there have been several new additions to EverQuest aimed at increasing the desirability and relative power of pure melee classes. The endurance system and the separation of the discipline timers have provided us with new tools to add interesting and powerful abilities in the future for melee classes. Unfortunately this has left the knights with absolutely no role in the game any more. To rectify this we're implementing the following changes:<br><br>1: All Knights to get Defensive and Stonewall disciplines.<br><br>2: Paladins to get Fortitude and Evasive disciplines.<br><br>3: Shadowknights to get Furious and Rampage disciplines.<br><br>4: All Knights to get a 4% universal damage reduction, Warriors retain their position as top tank with 5% reduction.<br><br>5: A line of self buffs to add agro procs to weapons will be be added, starting with +150 agro at level 30, scaling to +950 agro procs at the highest level.<br><br>6: The Furious Bash effect will be enhanced and have additional damage to bring it into line with dual wielding an offhand weapon.<br><br>These changes are designed to bring Knights back to their proper position relative to warriors.<br><br>- The EverQuest Team <br><br>参考URL<br>http://www.thesteelwarrior.org/forum/showthread.php?t=6469
</td>
